$DATUM 3-Formyl-1-(4-methoxy-benzyloxymethyl)-7-aza-bicyclo[2.2.1]heptane-7-carboxylic
acid tert-butyl ester (24). To a solution of oxalyl chloride (1507 μL,
17.57 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (80 mL) was added DMSO (1664 μL, 23.43 mmol) at-78
°C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 20 min and a solution of 23
(1474.2 mg, 3.906 mmol, obtained in the above reaction) in CH2Cl2 (40 mL)
was added at -78 °C. The reaction mixture was stirred for 40 min at -78
°C, and then Et3N (6.6 mL, 46.96 mmol) was added. The solution was
allowed to warm to rt. After 1 h stirring, the reaction mixture was
quenched by the addition of water. The mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2
(100 mL×3). The combined organic phase was washed with brine, dried over
Na2SO4, and the solvent was evaporated. Column chromatography (n-hexane /
AcOEt = 6 / 1) gave compound 24 (1522.5 mg, 100%, endo/exo = 82/18
mixture) as a colorless oil. 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): 9.731 (0.82H, d, J=
1.40 Hz,-CHO of endo isomer), 9.651 (0.18H, d, J= 1.80 Hz,-CHO of exo
isomer), 7.264 (2H, d, J= 8.64 Hz), 6.872 (2H, d, J= 8.72 Hz)[H aromatic
×4], 4.615-4.587 (1H, m, H-C(4)), 4.537-4.533 (2H, s,-O-CH2-C6H4OMe),
4.052-3.959 (2H, m, -CH2-OPMB), 3.806 (3H, s,-OCH3), 3.091-3.038 (0.82H,
m, H-C(3) of endo isomer), 2.529-2.491 (0.18H, m, H-C(3) of exo isomer),
2.141-2.098 (1H, m), 1.918-1.640 (4H, m), 1.533-1.453 (1H, m),[CH2 ×3],
1.439 (7.38H, s,-C(CH3)3 of endo isomer), 1.394 (1.62H, s, -C(CH3)3 of
exo isomer). MS (ESI,[M+Na]+): 398.
