$DATUM (S, E)-4-((2R,
6R)-6-ethyl-5-methyl-3,6-dihydro-2H-pyran-2-yl)-2-methylpent-3-enal. To a
cold suspension (0 ºC) of Dess-Martin periodinane (288 mg, 0.68 mmol) and
NaHCO3 (76 mg, 0.90 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (8 mL) was added a solution of
alcohol 32 (101 mg, 0.45 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (2 mL). The resulting mixture
was stirred for three hours at 0 ºC, then diluted with Et2O, and quenched
using a mixture of aqueous Na2S2O3·5H2O solution and saturated NaHCO3.
Stirring was continued until a clear organic layer was obtained. The
layers were separated and the aqueous phase was extracted with Et2O. The
combined organic phase was washed with brine, dried (MgSO4), and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude aldehyde (100 mg, 100% yield), obtained
as a colorless oil, was clean enough for use in the next step without
further purification. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.50 (d, J = 1.9 Hz, 1H),
5.59–5.55 (m, 1H), 5.31 (ddq, J = 8.9, 1.3, 1.3 Hz, 1H), 4.10 (br s, 1H),
3.90 (dd, J = 10.6, 3.0 Hz, 1H), 3.30 (dqd, J = 8.78, 6.90, 1.85 Hz, 1H),
2.15–2.05 (m, 1H), 1.83–1.74 (m, 1H), 1.98–1.90 (m, 1H), 1.73 (d, J = 1.3
Hz, 3H), 1.60 (ddd, J = 3.5, 1.2, 1.2 Hz, 3H), 1.58–1.48 (m, 1H), 1.18
(d, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H), 0.90 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
201.2, 141.2, 135.1, 120.6, 120.5, 78.0, 77.2, 45.8, 30.2, 25.6, 18.8,
13.9, 13.1, 8.2.
