$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure for the New Odorless Corey-Kim Oxidation Using Dodecyl
Methyl Sulfide (12) To 10 cm3 of a CH2Cl2 or toluene solution of 108 mg
of N-chlorosuccinimide (0.81 mmol) 2 cm3 of a CH2Cl2 or toluene solution
of 176 mg of 12 (0.81 mmol) were added dropwise at -40°C, and the
resulting mixture was stirred for 30 min. A CH2Cl2 or toluene solution (2
cm3)of 50mg of benzhydrol (0.27 mmol) was added dropwise at -40°C. After
the mixture was stirred for 2 h, 189 mm3 of triethylamine (1.36 mmol)
were added dropwise at -40°C. After stirring for 14 h, 20 cm3 of H2O were
added to the reaction mixture. The mixture was neutralised with 0.5 cm3
of 1 N HCl, followed by extraction of the aqueous layer with 3 x40 cm3 of
CHCl3 or 3 x40 cm3 of EtOAc. The combined organic layer was washed with
brine, dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. Silica gel
chromatography of the residue (n-hexane=EtOAc =40=1). 47 mg of
benzophenone (95% in CH2Cl2) or 49 mg (98% in toluene). A 20-times
scale-up experiment under the above conditions using 1.0 g of benzhydrol
(5.43 mmol) gave 953 mg of benzophenone (96%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-reagent, scalable, Corey-Kim oxidn., alternate prepn.
described
