$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Benzyloxymethyl-3-formyl-7-aza-bicyclo[2.2.1]heptane-7-carboxylic acid
tert-butyl ester (S3). To a solution of oxalyl chloride (1.5 mL, 17.49
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (200 mL) was added DMSO (1.6 mL, 22.53 mmol) at -78 °C.
The reaction mixture was stirred for 20 min and a solution of S2 (3.943
g, 11.35 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (250 mL) was added at -78 °C. The reaction
mixture was stirred for 40 min at -78 °C, and then Et3N (6.5 mL, 46.25
mmol) was added. The solution was allowed to warm to rt. After 1 h
stirring, the reaction mixture was quenched by addition of water. The
mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2 (300 mL×3). The combined organic phase
was washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, and the solvent was evaporated.
Column chromatography (n-hexane / AcOEt = 5 / 1) gave compound S3 (3.883
g, 99%, endo/exo = 82/18 mixture) as a colorless oil. 1H-NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): 9.739 (0.82H, d, J = 1.36 Hz,-CHO of endo isomer), 9.658 (0.18H,
d, J= 1.72 Hz,-CHO of exo isomer), 7.346-7.260 (5H, m,-Ph), 4.625-4.606
(3H, m, H-C(1) +-O-CH2-Ph), 4.091-3.997 (2H, m, -CH2-OCH2 Ph),
3.103-3.051 (0.82H, m, H-C(2) of endo isomer), 2.542-2.504 (0.18H, m,
H-C(2) of exo isomer), 2.188-1.455 (6H, m, CH2 ×3), 1.437 (7.38H,
s,-C(CH3)3of endo isomer), 1.391 (1.62H, s,-C(CH3)3 of exo isomer). MS
(ESI,[M+Na]+): 368.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Water-Stable Helical Structure of Tertiary Amides of Bicyclic β-Amino
Acid Bearing 7-Azabicyclo[2.2.1]heptane. Full Control of Amide Cis-Trans
Equilibrium by Bridgehead Substitution
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
