$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Diketone 3: A flask was charged with keto-alcohol S2 (395.8 mg, 1.36
mmol), CH2Cl2 (12 mL), pyridine (1.5 mL, 18.6 mmol), and Dess-Martin
periodinane (1.22 g, 2.88 mmol). The reaction was stirred at room
temperature for 30 min and then quenched with a saturated solution of 5:1
Na2S2O3:NaHCO3 (10 mL). The layers were separated, and the aqueous layer
was extracted further with CH2Cl2 (2 × 15 mL). The combined organic
extracts were dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated. Purification
by column chromatography (10% EtOAc/Hexanes) afforded diketone 3 (385 mg,
1.34 mmol) as a white crystalline solid in 99% yield. [α]24D = -58.5 (c =
0.33, CH2Cl2); IR (film) 2928, 1698 (str), 1437, 1228, 1077 cm-1; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.71 (s, 3H), 1.77-1.88 (m, 1H), 1.83 (s, 3H), 1.87
(d, J = 5.2 Hz, 1H), 1.97-2.01 (m, 1H), 2.06-2.14 (m, 1H), 2.30 (dt, J =
3.2, 12.4, 12.4 Hz, 1H), 2.40 (dt, J = 6.4, 12.4, 12.4 Hz, 1H), 2.45-2.49
(m, 2H), 2.64 (t, J = 8.0, 8.0 Hz, 1H), 2.81 (ddd, J = 3.2, 5.6, 12.4 Hz,
2H), 3.18 (dd, J = 7.2, 12.0 Hz, 2H), 4.17 (s, 1H), 4.51 (m, 1H), 4.85
(s, 2H), 5.53 (dd, J = 5.6, 11.2 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ
18.9, 26.2, 27.0, 29.4, 35.3, 38.5, 42.2, 44.3, 45.6, 52.3, 82.2, 89.0,
113.3, 127.2, 133.9, 146.0, 209.5, 213.1; MS (ESI+) for C18H24O3 [M+Na]+
calc 311.1 found 311.1.
