$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Dibenzylamino-5-oxo-pentanoic Acid Benzyl Ester (2); Typical Procedure
A solution of anhyd DMSO (3.0 g, 38 mmol) in anhyd CH2Cl2(18 mL) was
slowly added to a flask cooled to -78 °C containing oxalyl chloride (2.56
g, 20 mmol) in anhyd CH2Cl2 (37 mL) under N2 and magnetic stirring. The
mixture was stirred for 15 min, then a solution of the alcohol 4 (6.43 g,
16 mmol) in anhyd CH2Cl2 (10 mL) was slowly added. After stirring for 15
min, anhyd Et3N (5.3 mL) was added and the mixture was stirred for 15 min
at -78 °C. Additional Et3N (5 mL) was added and the flask was transferred
into a bath cooled to 0 °C and the mixture stirred for 15 min. Water (50
mL) was added, the mixture warmed to r.t. and the organic phase
separated. The aqueous phase was extracted several times with CH2Cl2, all
the organic fractions collected and washed with a 1 M HCl solution, a
sat. NaHCO3 solution and with brine. After drying over anhyd Na2SO4, the
solvent was evaporated to give aldehyde 2, determined via 1H, 13C and
ES/MS analyses. Viscous oil, yield 6.5 g, 99%. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3): δ
= 2.05 (m, 2 H), 2.5 (m, 2 H), 3.40 (t, J = 7 Hz, 1 H), 3.65 (d, J = 16
Hz, 2 H), 2.94 (d, J = 16 Hz, 2 H), 5.35 (AB system, 2 H), 7.1-7.4 (m, 15
H), 9.58 (ca s, 1 H). 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 21.6, 40.4, 54.5 (2 ×
C), 59.8, 66.2, 127.1, 128.3 (2 × C), 128.4 (2 × C), 128.5 (2 × C), 128.6
(2 × C), 128.9 (2 × C), 139.6, 172.0, 201.3. MS (ES): m/z = 424 [M+ +
Na].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Swern oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A simple procedure for the transformation of L-glutamic acid into the
corresponding γ-aldehyde
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Rodriquez, Manuela; Taddei, Maurizio
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2005), (3), 493-495

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME33 STEP1
$RXN



