$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: tert-Butyl
3-oxo-1-oxa-7-azaspiro[4.4]nonane-7-carboxylate (VIc). Dimethyl
sulfoxide, 21.8 g (0.28 mol), was added at -70°C to a solution of 17.9 g
(0.14 mol) of oxalyl chloride in 100 ml of anhydrous methylene chloride,
the mixture was stirred for 0.5 h, a solution of 24.3 g (0.1 mol) of
compound Vc in 80 ml of anhydrous methylene chloride was added at -70°C,
the mixture was stirred for 1 h, 31.4 g (0.31 mol) of triethylamine in
100 ml of methylene chloride was added, and the mixture was stirred for
0.5 h at -70°C and for 15 h at room temperature. The dark organic
solution was washed with two portions of 20% aqueous citric acid and
dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate, and the solvent was distilled off
under reduced pressure. Yield 23.4 g (97%). mp 71-72°C (from hexane).IR
spectrum, ν, cm-1: 1730, 1691 (C═O). 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 1.42 s (9H,
t-Bu), 1.92-2.13 m (2H, CH2), 2.50 s (2H, CH2C═O), 3.31 m and 3.51 m (2H
each, NCH2), 3.98 s (2H, OCH2). Mass spectrum: m/z 142 [M - 101 + H]+.
Found, %: C 59.68; H 7.63; N 5.66. C12H19NO4. Calculated, %: C 59.75; H
7.88; N 5.81. M 241.
