$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: tert-Butyl
3-oxo-1-oxa-7-azaspiro[4.4]nonane-7-carboxylate (VIc). Dimethyl
sulfoxide, 21.8 g (0.28 mol), was added at -70°C to a solution of 17.9 g
(0.14 mol) of oxalyl chloride in 100 ml of anhydrous methylene chloride,
the mixture was stirred for 0.5 h, a solution of 24.3 g (0.1 mol) of
compound Vc in 80 ml of anhydrous methylene chloride was added at -70°C,
the mixture was stirred for 1 h, 31.4 g (0.31 mol) of triethylamine in
100 ml of methylene chloride was added, and the mixture was stirred for
0.5 h at -70°C and for 15 h at room temperature. The dark organic
solution was washed with two portions of 20% aqueous citric acid and
dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate, and the solvent was distilled off
under reduced pressure. tert-Butyl
3-oxo-1-oxa-8-azaspiro[4.5]decane-8-carboxylate (VIe). Yield 97%. mp
65-66°C (from hexane).IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 1738, 1692 (C═O). 1H NMR
spectrum, δ, ppm: 1.40 s (9H, t-Bu), 1.54- 1.73 m (4H, CH2), 2.42 s (2H,
CH2C═O), 3.31 m and 3.45 m (2H each, NCH2), 3.99 s (2H, OCH2). Mass
spectrum: m/z 156 [M - 101 + H]+. Found, %: C 61.09; H 8.17; N 5.28.
C13H21NO4. Calculated, %: C 61.18; H 8.24; N 5.49. M 255.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Swern oxidn., in-situ generated reagent in first stage
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM General procedure for the synthesis of spirocyclic 3-hydroxy- and
3-oxotetrahydrofurans containing carbo- and heterocyclic fragments
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Moskalenko, A. I.; Belopukhov, S. L.; Ivlev, A. A.; Boev, V. I.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of Organic Chemistry (2011), 47(7), 1091-1096

