$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for the New Odorless
Corey-Kim Oxidation Using Dodecyl Methyl Sulfide (12) To 10 cm3 of a
CH2Cl2 or toluene solution of 108 mg of N-chlorosuccinimide (0.81 mmol) 2
cm3 of a CH2Cl2 or toluene solution of 176 mg of 12 (0.81 mmol) were
added dropwise at -40°C, and the resulting mixture was stirred for 30
min. A CH2Cl2 or toluene solution (2 cm3)of 50mg of benzhydrol (0.27
mmol) was added dropwise at -40°C. After the mixture was stirred for 2 h,
189 mm3 of triethylamine (1.36 mmol) were added dropwise at -40°C. After
stirring for 14 h, 20 cm3 of H2O were added to the reaction mixture. The
mixture was neutralised with 0.5 cm3 of 1 N HCl, followed by extraction
of the aqueous layer with 3 x40 cm3 of CHCl3 or 3 x40 cm3 of EtOAc. The
combined organic layer was washed with brine, dried (Na2SO4), filtered,
and concentrated in vacuo. Silica gel chromatography of the residue
(n-hexane=EtOAc =40=1). 47 mg of benzophenone (95% in CH2Cl2) or 49 mg
(98% in toluene).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-reagent, Corey-Kim oxidn., alternate solvent gives
similar yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Development of Odorless Thiols and Sulfides and Their Applications to
Organic Synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Nishide, Kiyoharu; Ohsugi, Shin-ichi; Miyamoto, Tetsuo; Kumar, Kamal;
Node, Manabu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Monatshefte fuer Chemie (2004), 135(2), 189-200

