$DATUM 2,2-Bis-benzyloxymethyl-3-{O-(2,3,4,6-tetra-O-acetyl-β-D-galactopyranosyl)-(1
→ 4)-O-[2,3,6-tri-O-benzyl-α-L-fucopyranosyl)-(1 →
3)]-2-acetamido-6-O-benzyl-2-deoxy-β-D-glucopyranosyloxy}-propanal (9).
DMSO (81.5 µL, 1.15 mmol) was added dropwise to a cooled (-78°C) solution
of oxalyl chloride (20 µL) in CH2Cl2 (500 µL). After 15 min, a solution
of compound 8 (97 mg, 77 µmol) in CH2Cl2 (0.5 mL) was added and the
resulting mixture was stirred at -78°C for 30 min. Then, NEt3 (160 µL,
1.15 mmol) was added and the reaction mixture was slowly warmed up to 0°C
over 3 h. The reaction was then diluted with CH2Cl2, washed with a 5% aq
solution of KH2PO4 then with water. The aq layers were extracted with
CH2Cl2. Then, the organic phases were pooled, filtered using silicone
treated paper, and concentrated. Flash chromatography of the residue
(EtOAc/petroleum ether, 1/1). 9 (94 mg, 96%) as a colorless syrup. [α]D
24 -53 (c 1.05, CH2Cl2). 1H NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.65 (s, 1 H, CHO),
7.45-7.15 (m, 30 H, Ph), 5.72 (d, 1 H, JNH,2 I = 8.5 Hz, NH), 5.27 (d, 1
H, J3 III,4 III = 3.5 Hz, H-4III), 5.04 (d, 1 H, J1 II,2 II = 3.5 Hz,
H-1II), 5.02 (dd, 1 H, J1 III,2 III = 8.6 Hz, J2 III,3 III = 11.0 Hz,
H-2III), 4.95 (d, 1 H, J = 12 Hz, CHPh), 4.85 (d, 1 H, J= 11.5 Hz, CHPh),
4.82 (d, I Η, H-3III), 4.76 (d, 1 H, CHPh), 4.70 (d, 1 H, J = 12 Hz,
CHPh), 4.69 (d, 1 H, JIV = 7.0 Hz, H-1I), 4.68 (d, 1 H, CHPh), 4.60 (d, 1
H, CHPh), 4.52 (d, 1 H, H-1III), 4.44 (s, 2 H, OCH2Ph), 4.39 (s, 2 H,
OCH2Ph), 4.38 (d, 1 H, CHPh), 4.32 (m, 1 H, H-5II), 4.12 (dd, 1 H, J5
III,6 III = 8.0 Hz, J6 III,6 III = 11.0 Hz, H-6III), 4.09 (d, 1H, J = 9.5
Hz), 4.09 (dd, 1 H, J2 II,3 II = 10.5 Hz, H-2II), 4.05 (t, 1 H, J2 I,3 I
= 7.0 Hz, J3 I,4 I = 7.0 Hz, H-3I), 3.97 (dd, 1 H, J5 III,6 III = 6.0 Hz,
H-6' III), 3.93 (t, 1 H, J4 I,5 I = 7.0 Hz, H-4I), 3.87 (dd, 1 H, J3 II,4
II = 2.5 Hz, H-3II), 3.80-3.53 (m, 10 H), 3.48 (m, 1 Η, H-5I), 2.00,
