$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Aldehyde Formation:5 Oxalyl chloride (18.0 μL, 0.21
mmol) was dissolved in dichloromethane (0.5 mL) and cooled to -78° C.
Dimethylsulfoxide (28.5 μL, 0.40 mmol) in 40 μl dichloromethane was added
and allowed to stir for 2 minutes. Primary alcohol S22(15.5 mg, 56.5
μmol) was added and the solution stirred at -78° C for 30 minutes.
Triethylamine (200 μL, 1.43 mmol) was added and the solution was stirred
for 30 minutes. Aqueous NaHCO3 (1.0 mL) was added while the solution was
still cold and allowed to stir at -78°C for 10 minutes before warming.
Once mixture was warm enough to melt aqueous layer the solution was
partitioned between aqueous NaHCO3 and CH2Cl2 and the aqueous layer
washed a second time with CH2Cl2. The combined organics were dried over
Na2SO4 and conc. in vacuo to give the crude aldehyde 15.0 mg (95%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Swern oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
