$DATUM 1.4 (R)-4,6-dimethylenanthal (3) Under the protection of argon gas, 15 mL
anhydrous dichloromethane and redistilled oxalyl chloride 0.36 mL (5
mmol) were added into a 100 mL reaction flask at -78 °C followed by slow
and dropwise addition of 0.60 mL (10 mmol) redistilled dimethyl sulfoxide
via a syringe. After 40 min, 15 mL of a solution of 0.61 g (4 mmol)
compound 6 in dichloromethane was added slowly dropwise over 15 min. The
reaction was performed for further 40 min. Anhydrous triethylamine 2.4 mL
(16 mol) was added dropwise via a constant-pressure funnel. The reaction
solution was then warmed naturally to room temperature, saturated sodium
bicarbonate solution added, and the solution separated. The aqueous phase
was extracted with dichloromethane (2 × 50 mL). The organic phases were
combined, washed twice with water then once with saturated salt water,
dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate and filtered. The solvent was removed
via rotary evaporation under reduced pressure, and the residue purified
by silica gel column chromatography [V (ethyl acetate) : V (petroleum
ether) = 1 : 25] to give the desired product as a greenish transparent
oily liquid (0.56 g, yield 94 %). (R)-4,6-dimethylenanthal (3), 94 %,
greenish transparent oily liquid [α]20D-3.95 (c 1.05, CHCl3); 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ: 9.71-9.70 (t, J = 2.7 Hz, 1H), 2.40-2.33 (m, 2H),
1.60-1.55 (m, 2H), 1.46-1.39 (m, 2H), 1.04-0.95 (m, 2H), 0.81-0.76 (m,
9H); IR (KBr) ν: 2958, 2931, 2907, 2872, 2718, 1730, 1468, 1119, 807;
EIMS m/z (%): 143 (M+ + 1, 8.01), 125 (4.57), 83 (48.97), 43 (100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
