$DATUM Methyl 8-(2-formyl-5-oxocyclopent-1-enyl)octanoate, 10a. To a cooled
(-78ºC) solution of oxalyl chloride (280 μL, 3.19 mmol) in 21 mL of dry
dichloromethane was added DMSO (450 μL, 6.36mmol) dropwise; the mixture
was stirred at this temperature for 30 min. Then, a solution of alcohol
8a (428 mg, 1.59 mmol) in 8 mL of dry dichloromethane was added dropwise
via cannula, and the resulting solution was stirred at -78 ºC for an
additional 1 h. Finally, 1.20 mL of triethylamine were added dropwise.
After 2 h stirring at - 78 ºC, the reaction mixture was allowed to warm
to room temperature slowly. The reaction was quenched by addition of
water and, after a few minutes stirring vigorously, the layers were
separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with dichloromethane. The
combined organics layers were washed with brine, dried over anhydrous
MgSO4, and evaporated. Flash chromatography (5:5 hexanes/ethyl acetate)
afforded 388 mg (92%) of 10a as a colourless oil. IR (film): υmax 2924,
2853, 1739, 1707, 1675, 1431, 1169 cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.30-
1.33 (m, 6H, CH2), 1.49-1.52 (m, 2H, CH2), 1.59-1.64 (m, 2H, CH2), 2.29
(t, J= 7.6 Hz, 2H, CH2), 2.42-2.50 (m, 2H, CH2), 2.57 (t, J= 7.6 Hz, 2H,
CH2), 2.68-2.70 (m, 2H, CH2), 3.66 (s, 3H, CH3), 10.38 (s, 1H, CHO) ppm.
13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 22.3 (CH2), 23.2 (CH2), 23.6 (CH2), 25.2
(CH2), 29.2 (CH2), 29.9 (CH2), 29.7 (CH2), 34.4 (CH2), 44.2 (CH2), 51.8
(CH3), 154.3 (C), 159.1 (C), 176.1 (C), 190.6 (C), 211.0 (C) ppm. MS (ESI
(+) H2O: CH3CN): m/z 235 [(M-CH3O)+, 22%], m/z 251 [(M-CH3)+, 50%]. HMRS
(ESI (+) H2O: CH3CN): calcd for C14H19O4: 251.1279; found: 251.1277.
