$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-(Adamantane-1-yl-methoxy)-1-pentanal (23). A solution of oxalylchloride
(789 μL, 9.02 mmol) in DCM (25 mL) was cooled to -78 °C. After dropwise
addition of a solution of DMSO (1.28 mL, 18.04 mmol) in DCM (8.2 mL), the
reaction mixture was stirred for 30 minutes while being kept below -70
°C. A dry solution of 22 (2.068 g, 8.20 mmol) in DCM (8.2 mL) was added
dropwise to the reaction mixture at -78 °C. After stirring the reaction
mixture for 2 hours, while being kept below -65 °C, Et3N (5.68 mL, 41
mmol) was added dropwise. The reaction mixture was allowed to warm to rt
over two hours. The reaction mixture was successively washed with 0.5M aq
citric acid (2×30 mL) and water (2×30 mL). The organic phase was dried
(Na2SO4), concentrated and the resulting residue was purified by flash
silica gel column chromatography (5%→ 15% EtOAc in PE) to give product 23
(8.816 g, 25.75 mmol) in 92% yield as a pale yellow oil.
5-(Adamantane-1-yl-methoxy)-1-pentanal (23)., yield (8.816 g, 25.75
mmol),92% Rf = 0.70 (1:3; EtOAc:PE). 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 9.78
(s, 1H), 3.39 (t, JH-H = 5.9 Hz, 2H), 2.95 (s, 2H), 2.47 (dt, JH-H = 1.4
Hz, JH-H = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 1.95 (br s, 3H), 1.76-1.52 (m, 16H). 13C NMR (50
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 202.4, 81.8, 70.8, 43.5, 39.6, 37.1, 33.9, 28.8, 28.1,
18.8. ATR-IR (thin film): 2900.7, 2846.7, 2715.6, 1728.1, 1450.4, 1404.1,
1357.8, 1257.5, 1226.6, 1157.2, 1103.2, 1056.9, 1010.6, 941.2, 887.2,
810.0, 655.8 cm-1. HRMS: found 251.1998 [M+H]+, calculated for
[C16H26O2+H]+ 253.2006.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Development of Adamantan-1-yl-methoxy-Functionalized 1-Deoxynojirimycin
Derivatives as Selective Inhibitors of Glucosylceramide Metabolism in Man
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
