$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method B. Dess-Martin Oxidation A soln of
alcohol 23 (3.71 g 10.0 mmol), 25 (4.47 g, 10.0 mmol), 31 (4.57 g, 10.0
mmol), or 32 (5.33 g, 10.0 mmol) in anhyd CH2Cl2 (20 mL) was added
dropwise to a stirred soln of 12-I-5-triacetoxyperiodinane (10.60 g, 25.0
mmol), solid NaHCO3 (1.6 g), and molecular sieves (4 Å, 15 g) in anhyd
CH2Cl2 (400 mL) at 0 °C under an Ar atmosphere. After stirring for 4 h at
r.t. (reaction monitored by TLC), solids were filtered off, and the
filtrate was concentrated. The residue was purified by flash
chromatography to provide the ethynyl ketones 27,29,33, and 34.
1-(5-O-tert-Butyldimethylsilyl-2,3-O-isopropylidene-1-deoxy-β-D-ribofuranos-1-yl)pent-4-yn-3-one
(27) Method B. Purified by flash chromatography (solvent A8).
1-(5-O-tert-Butyldimethylsilyl-2,3-O-isopropylidene-1-deoxy-β-D-ribofuranos-1-yl)-5-phenyl-pent-4-yn-3-one
(29) Method B. Purified by flash chromatography (solvent A10).
1-(5-O-tert-Butyldimethylsilyl-2,3-O-isopropylidene-1-deoxy-β-D-ribofuranos-1-yl)-5-phenyl-pent-4-yn-3-one
(29), Yield: 4.0 g (90%); pale-yellow syrup [a]D23 -28.0 (c 1.0, CH2Cl2);
Rf= 0.39 (solvent A6). 1H NMR (300.13 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.06, 0.07 [2 x s,
6 H, Si(CH3)2], 0.89 [s, 9 H, C(CH3)3], 1.34, 1.52 [2 x s, 6 H, C(CH3)2],
1.89-2.12 (m, 2 H, H-1), 2.72-2.91 (m, 2 H, H-2), 3.71 (m, 2 H,
H-5'),3.91 (app dt, 3J1a,1' = 8.0 Hz, 3J1b,1' ≈ 3J1',2' = 5.0 Hz, 1 H,
H-1'), 4.01 (app q, 3J3',4' ≈ 3J4',5' = 3.5 Hz, 1'H, H-4'), 4.31 (dd,
3J2',3' = 6.6 Hz, 3J1',2' = 5.0 Hz, 1 H, H-2'), 4.64 (dd, 3J2',3' = 6.6
Hz, 3J3',4' = 3.5 Hz, 1 H, H-3'), 7.34-7.48 (m, 3 H, m-,p-Ph), 7.55-7.58
(m, 2 H, o-Ph). 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3): δ = -5.4, -5.3 [Si(CH3)2],
18.3 [C(CH3)3], 25.5, 27.5 [C(CH3)2], 25.9 [C(CH3)3], 27.8 (C-1), 41.6
(C-2), 63.6 (C-5'), 81.9 (C-3'), 83.4, 84.5, 84.8 (C-1',2',4'), 87.7
(C-4), 90.7 (C-5), 114.0 [C(CH3)2], 120.0 (i-Ph), 128.6 (m-Ph), 130.6
(p-Ph), 133.0 (o-Ph), 186.9 (C-3). Anal. Calcd for C25H36O5Si (444.64):
C, 67.53; H, 8.16. Found: C, 67.62; H, 8.30.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM key intermediate for the synthesis of heterocyclic systems, Dess-Martin
oxidation, molecular sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A versatile approach to alcohol, aldehyde, ketone and amine derivatives
starting from β-allyl C-glycosides of D-ribofuranose and
2-deoxy-D-ribofuranose
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Waechtler, Heike; Fuentes, Dilver Pena; Michalik, Dirk; Koeckerling,
Martin; Villinger, Alexander; Kragl, Udo; Cedeno, Quirino Arias; Vogel,
Christian
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2011), (19), 3099-3108

