$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Diisobutylnaphthalodioxole dialdehyde (5a) In a dry 100 mL round-bottom
flask with a large stir magnet was added 20 mL methylene chloride and
1.51 mL oxalyl chloride (17.6 mmol, 3 eq.). The reaction was cooled to
-78°C under N2 and a mixture of 2.5 mL DMSO in 5 mL methylene chloride
was added dropwise. It was stirred an additional 5 minutes before a
mixture of dimethanol 4a (2.00 g, 5.81 mmol, 1 eq.) in 15 mL methylene
chloride was added dropwise and stirred 20 minutes. An additional 20 mL
methylene chloride was then added dropwise to the thick solution and
stirred an additional 40 minutes. Triethylamine (13 mL, 93 mmol, 16 eq.)
was then added dropwise and the mixture was slowly warmed to room
temperature and washed with 50 mL ice water. The aqueous layer was
extracted 3x with methylene chloride and the combined organic layers were
dried once with NaCl brine. The solution was dried with MgSO4, filtered,
and solvent was removed with rotary evaporation. The material was eluted
through a silica gel plug with methylene chloride. Yield 1.79 g, 90%. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 10.59 (s, 2H), 8.22 (s, 2H), 7.20 (s, 2H), 1.87
(d, J = 4.8 Hz, 4H), 1.86 (m, 2H), 0.97 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 12H). 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 192.8, 151.9, 132.8, 132.6, 131.6, 124.2, 104.9, 46.9,
24.1, 23.7. MS (EI 70 eV) m/z 340 (M+, 50%), 283 (M+ - 57, 100%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Swern oxidation, incremental addition solvent stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Optical Properties of Dioxolane-Functionalized Hexacenes
and Heptacenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Bruzek, Matthew J.; Anthony, John E.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(13), 3608-3610

