$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4.3. 1-[(Dimethyl)(phenyl)silyl]prop-2-yn-1-one (7d). Jones reagent (1.90
mL, 5.07 mmol) was added dropwise at -80 °C to a stirred solution of
(±)-3d (814 mg, 4.28 mmol). The mixture was allowed to slowly warm to -50
°C. It was quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution, and after
extraction with Et2O and chromatography (hexane/Et2O, 10: 1), 7d (709 mg,
3.76 mmol, 88%) was obtained as a yellowish oil. IR: 3370m, 3070w, 3050w,
2960w, 2070s, 1730w, 1605s, 1460m, 1250s, 1115s, 1020m, 950m, 840s, 815s,
790s, 740s, 710s, 700s. 1H NMR: 7.62-7.35 (m, 5 arom. H); 3.81 (s, CH);
0.58 (2s, Me2Si). 13C NMR: 224.1 (s); 134.2 (d, 2C); 132.6 (s); 130.3
(d); 128.1 (d, 2C); 86.7 (d); 84.3 (s); -5.3 (q, 2C). CI-MS: 206 (100, [M
+ NH4]+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Jones reagent used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective Synthesis of Di-, Tri-, and Tetrasubstituted
Allenylsilanes
