$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: GENERAL PROCEDURE DMSO (4 mmol) was added to a
solution of phosphonitrilic chloride (1.0 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (5 mL) at
-40°C. The color of the solution turned milky white. After 1 h, 1
equivalent of an alcohol solution in CH2Cl2 (2 mL) was added, and the
reaction mixture was stirred at the same temperature for 45 min, when
Et3N (5 mmol) was added. The reaction mixture was slowly allowed to come
to rt (8 h). The reaction mixture was taken in CH2Cl2 and washed with
water and brine. The organic layer was dried over Na2SO4 and condensed.
The crude product was chromatographed over silica gel by column
chromatography to provide pure ketones in high yields (Table 1). All the
carbonyl compounds are either commercially available or known in
literature. They were characterized by the usual spectral data and
compared with authentic samples. Cyclododecanone, yield 86%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Activation of DMSO by phosphonitrilic chloride. An efficient method for
oxidation of alcohols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pandey, Sanjay K.; Bisai, Alakesh; Singh, Vinod K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2007), 37(23), 4099-4103

