$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Diethylnaphthalodioxole dialdehyde (5b) In a dry 250 mL round-bottom
flask equipped with a large stirring magnet was added 40 mL methylene
chloride and oxalyl chloride (3.02 mL, 35.2 mmol, 3 eq.) and cooled under
nitrogen to -78°C. DMSO (5 mL, 70.3 mmol, 6 eq.) was dissolved in 10 mL
methylene chloride and added dropwise. The mixture was stirred an
additional 5 minutes before adding dropwise over ~15 min diol 4b (3.38 g,
11.7 mmol, 1 eq.) dissolved in 30 mL methylene chloride + 5 mL DMSO. The
solution was stirred for 20 minutes before adding an additional 40 mL
methylene chloride slowly over ~3 minutes and stirring an additional 30
minutes. Triethylamine (26 mL, 15.9 eq.) was added and the solution was
allowed to warm to room temperature. The mixture was washed with 70 mL
ice water and the aqueous layer extracted 3x with methylene chloride. The
combined organic layers were dried with MgSO4, filtered, and solvent was
removed with rotary evaporation. The material was eluted through a silica
gel plug with methylene chloride. Yield 2.82 g, 85%. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 10.58 (s, 2H), 8.21 (s, 2H), 7.20 (s, 2H), 2.02 (q, J = 7.4 Hz,
4H), 1.01 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 6H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 192.8, 152.3,
132.8, 132.6, 131.5, 124.1, 104.6, 31.0, 7.1. MS (EI 70 eV) m/z 284 (M+,
25%), 255 (M+ - 29, 20%), 227 (M+ - 57, 100%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Swern oxidation, incremental addition solvent stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Optical Properties of Dioxolane-Functionalized Hexacenes
and Heptacenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
